stom  response header we added gcp-status  with the value hit  this means that the response was served  from a gcp edge cache and not from the  bucket directly  by using cloud cdn you're able to  improve origin offload and reduce egress  costs  while simultaneously increasing the  response speed for the end user  to test that cloud armor is working we  can send a curl request including the  header name evil header  we configured the cloud armor security  policy with a rule that explicitly  blocks traffic with this header  the response from the curl is a 403  forbidden which is exactly what we  expected and consistent with what was  configured  thank you for listening to this  presentation and demo we hope you found  it useful  please add your questions to the  comments if you have any  thanks

